From 1661c31429ea38fe728911334bf62a014a09c23b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:00:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] port 674fbe41: generate: --vision with --batch refuses to
 mix image and text rows (one M-RoPE table per device)

The image position table (mrope.hpp) is one per device and is rebuilt at every GEN/GENI admission, while every batch
row reads it at its own slot's cell.  An image slot decoding next to text slots gave them its positions and took
theirs: silently wrong text in both (upstream behaviour, any --batch > 1 with --vision).

Until the table is kept per slot, the engine refuses the mix instead of decoding it wrong, with an ERR line and no
state touched: a GENI/BGENI while any batch slot is active ("ERR vision: an image request is not taken while batch
slot <b> decodes ..."), and a GEN/BGEN while an active slot was admitted with images (BSlot::img).  Without --vision,
or with only text requests, nothing changes.  The server's image gate (next commit) keeps the refusal unreachable in
normal operation.

Port to v0.2.12: the check sits where it did, after the prefill-only check and the req_df2 policy swap (the GEN/GENI
parse moved by ~3300 lines), before the M-RoPE table is rebuilt.  BSlot::img and the rest are unchanged upstream.  A
refused BGEN leaves co_set to the next BGEN (it reassigns it), so a pending BCO co-read is not run on a refused line.

(cherry picked from commit 674fbe411c156dd61659bb0c31d2acf1bc749695)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/program/generate.cpp | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/program/generate.cpp b/src/program/generate.cpp
index 03113d5a..127c36af 100644
--- a/src/program/generate.cpp
+++ b/src/program/generate.cpp
@@ -15859,6 +15859,32 @@ int main(int argc, char** argv) {
             }
             req_imgs.clear();
             if (geni && !o.vision) { std::printf("ERR this engine was started without --vision\n"); continue; }
+            // --vision with --batch: the M-RoPE table below is one per device, indexed by a cell's position, and every
+            // batch row reads it at its slot's own position.  An image request's table is not the identity a text
+            // slot needs (nor another image slot's), so image and text rows never decode together: a GENI / BGENI
+            // only while no slot decodes, a GEN / BGEN not while a slot that was admitted with pictures decodes.
+            // (Before the table is touched; text-only traffic never meets either refusal.)
+            if (o.vision && !bs.empty()) {
+                int busy = -1, busy_img = -1;
+                for (size_t b = 0; b < bs.size(); ++b) {
+                    if (!bs[b].active) continue;
+                    if (busy < 0) busy = (int) b;
+                    if (busy_img < 0 && bs[b].img) busy_img = (int) b;
+                }
+                if (geni && busy >= 0) {
+                    std::printf("ERR vision: an image request is not taken while batch slot %d decodes (image and text "
+                                "rows share one M-RoPE table); try again once the slots are idle\n", busy);
+                    std::fflush(stdout);
+                    continue;
+                }
+                if (!geni && busy_img >= 0) {
+                    std::printf("ERR vision: a text request is not taken while batch slot %d decodes an image "
+                                "request (image and text rows share one M-RoPE table); try again once it ends\n",
+                                busy_img);
+                    std::fflush(stdout);
+                    continue;
+                }
+            }
             if (geni || !mrope_identity) {
                 // positions for every cell this request can reach; the identity again for a text request
                 std::string ve;
